  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "IMSECH forms the scaled reciprocal of IMCOSH(z) without EXP's real-axis overflow check, returning \"0\" at 1e100",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, IMSECH(inumber) computes cosh(inumber) via hyperbolic_parts (with 0.0001 Taylor 1 + re^2/2 and 20.0 EXP(|re|)/2 cutoffs) without IMCOSH's real-axis EXP-overflow #NUM! check, then forms the single scaled reciprocal 1 / cosh(z) with subnormal components flushed to 0 (so IMSECH(1e100) returns \"0\"). All 1,224 full-bank IMSECH rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence cache/w111-extended-regenerated-20260929/answers-imsech.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430) and Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (prefix_metadata row 129); 1,224/1,224 full-bank rows match.",
